        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital admission of your 84-year-old male patient from 12th to 13th October 2025. He was admitted due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, clinical examination revealed reduced air entry bilaterally with expiratory wheeze, and oxygen saturation was diminished on room air. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation consistent with COPD. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and received intravenous fluids for supportive care. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. At discharge, he was stable on room air. Please continue inhaled maintenance therapy and ensure outpatient follow-up. Smoking cessation counselling was reinforced. Kind regards, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
